Nexsland is an independent GNOME Shell extension. Apart from lib/bar/ (Open
Bar, below), it contains no code or assets copied from these projects; their
designs informed its behavior.

- DynamicNotch (https://github.com/jackson-storm/DynamicNotch), GPL-3.0.
  The live-activity / temporary-notification presentation model in
  lib/engine/engine.js follows its NotchEngine design.
- Atoll (https://github.com/Ebullioscopic/Atoll), GPL-3.0, itself derived
  from boring.notch (https://github.com/TheBoredTeam/boring.notch), GPL-3.0.
  Feature set and interaction ideas.
- Open Bar (https://github.com/neuromorph/openbar) by neuromorph,
  GPL-2.0-or-later / GPL-3.0. lib/bar/ is Open Bar's source (upstream commit
  01fb242, its GNOME 49 release), adapted to run as Nexsland's Bar module and
  continued past GNOME 49, and cut down to styling the top bar and its island
  buttons. Changes are marked "Nexsland:" in the code. Its menu, dash,
  notification, wallpaper-palette and GTK/Flatpak theming, its preferences and
  its media are not included.
- NexTile (https://github.com/fresp/nexTile), GPL-3.0-or-later.
  Build, lint and logging scaffolding, and the no-untracked-connect ESLint rule.

